  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The capacity of the institutions for the resolution and prevention of labour disputes in Barbados has been strengthened through the adoption of measures included in a tripartite action plan based on results of the self-assessment diagnostic tool. For example, by increasing the independence of the Employment Rights Tribunals as an autonomous body (detached from the labour ministry). These measures improve the capacity of institutions to respond to the demand for the provision of their conflict resolution services. In September 2022, the ILO has facilitated the implementation of the self-assessment diagnostic tool for the effectiveness of conflict resolution institutions, at the Employment Rights Tribunal at the request of the Ministry of Labour of Barbados. As a result of these interventions, a tripartite action plan was adopted to generate improvement measures.</narrative>
   </description>
